<header><div class="eyebrow">MBTX RESEARCH / REPRODUCIBLE EVIDENCE</div><h1>Programmable workflow study</h1><p id="identity"></p><div id="badges"></div></header>
<nav aria-label="Report views"><button data-view="overview" aria-current="page">Overview</button><button data-view="tasks">Task comparison</button><button data-view="compare">Paired trajectories</button><button data-view="detail">Step details</button><button data-view="method">Method &amp; evidence</button></nav>
<main><p id="error" role="alert" hidden></p>
<section id="overview"><h2>Completion before efficiency</h2><p>All assigned samples remain in the denominator. Step comparisons describe the subset where both arms completed successfully with complete step evidence.</p><div id="metrics" class="cards"></div><div id="completion-chart" class="chart" role="img" aria-label="Assigned arm outcomes"></div><h3>Basic and complexity tracks</h3><p>Each track keeps its assigned denominator, including failed and unstarted arms. The two repetitions belong to the same task; they are not independent tasks.</p><div id="track-summary" class="scroll"></div><h3>Actual decision steps by track</h3><p>Both tracks include every captured outcome with a known total, including failures. Unknown totals remain separate from their observed prefixes; these distributions do not pool the two tracks.</p><div id="track-step-distributions" class="scroll"></div><h3>Conditional paired estimates</h3><div id="estimates"></div><h3>Actual decision steps in the complexity track</h3><p>All captured outcomes contribute when their total is known. Unknown totals retain their observed prefixes in the evidence. Design ranges are calibration targets, never required minimums.</p><div id="step-distributions" class="scroll"></div><h3>Repeated attempts on the same task</h3><p>Repeats are nested within fixed tasks. A difference records variation; it does not identify its cause. Failed attempts have no steps-to-success value.</p><div id="repeat-comparisons" class="scroll"></div><h3>Observed interaction costs</h3><p>Reference pages, compiler and runtime failures, and external retries are separate observations. Activities may overlap in one decision; first successful compilation is not task completion or a repair-step count.</p><div id="interaction-summary" class="scroll"></div><h3>Execution evidence</h3><p>Compiler starts, program launches and runtime denial messages are separate observations. Runtime denial messages do not provide a complete child-process audit; child-process totals remain unknown.</p><div id="execution-evidence"></div><h3>Scope of the evidence</h3><ul id="limits"></ul></section>
<section id="tasks" hidden><h2>Task comparison</h2><div id="filters" class="filters"></div><p id="filter-count" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="pair-chart" class="chart" role="img" aria-label="Observed paired step differences"></div><div class="scroll"><table id="task-table"></table></div></section>
<section id="compare" hidden><h2>Paired trajectories</h2><label>Pair <select id="pair-select"></select></label><label>View <select id="axis"><option value="steps">Decision sequence</option><option value="time">Relative monotonic time</option></select></label><p>Step N in one arm is not assumed to match step N in the other. Each lane retains its own decision sequence. Missing or incompatible clocks remain unknown.</p><div id="timelines" class="lanes"></div></section>
<section id="detail" hidden><h2>Step details</h2><p>Select a step from a trajectory. Original output previews, complete resources and source snapshots are preserved separately.</p><div id="step-detail"></div></section>
<section id="method" hidden><h2>Method &amp; evidence</h2><p>Observed fields come from retained evidence. Repair intent and causal explanations require interpretation. No model-private reasoning or relay-internal timing is available.</p><button id="export-model">Export complete analysis JSON</button><div id="method-content"></div></section>
</main><footer>Offline artifact · Apache ECharts 6.0.0 · No external services · Native trace and raw evidence remain authoritative.</footer><noscript>This report needs JavaScript for local decompression and filtering. report.json, report.md and report.csv remain available beside this file.</noscript>
